aligned_segments.en:
It is the aspect of the sea, into which all the rivers flow, as it is written (Ecclesiastes 1): All the rivers go to the sea (see Tikkun 11 from the later

Tikkunim

).

It is brought (Midrash Tanchuma, parsha

Bereishit

): And Hashem set for Cain a sign, that a horn shone for him, as above.

East [

kidmat

] is the initials of "forehead that does not lay tefillin" (see Rosh Hashanah 17a).
